{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואתכם אזרה", :translit "v'etchem ezareh", :gloss "and you I will scatter"} {:he "הזי\"ן עקומה", :translit "hazayin ikumah", :gloss "the zayin is bent"} {:he "ארץ ז' עממין", :translit "eretz zayin ammin", :gloss "land of seven nations"} {:he "שחצבה עמודיה שבעה", :translit "shechatzvah amudeha shiv'ah", :gloss "whose pillars He hewed out as seven"} {:he "ואתם שבעה תועבות בלבבכם", :translit "v'atem shiv'ah to'evot bilvavchem", :gloss "and you seven abominations in your hearts"} {:he "לכך אתכם אזרה", :translit "lachach etchem ezareh", :gloss "therefore you I will scatter"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The bent form of the letter zayin in 'ואתכם אזרה' signals a hidden link to the concept of seven (zayin = 7): seven nations, seven pillars of Torah, seven abominations."}], :frame {:text "Wisdom is described as having hewn out her seven pillars (Proverbs 9:1), which is read as a reference to the Torah and its seven books or foundational principles. Joshua is told the Israelites will possess the land of seven nations (Deuteronomy 7:1). Proverbs 26:25 speaks of seven abominations in the heart.", :sources ["Proverbs 9:1" "Deuteronomy 7:1" "Proverbs 26:25"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והריקותי", :translit "v'harikoti", :gloss "and I will make desolate"} {:he "והריקותי לכם ברכה עד בלי די", :translit "v'harikoti lachem berachah ad bli dai", :gloss "and I will empty out for you blessing until without enough"} {:he "ואתם לא רציתם לקיים מצותי", :translit "v'atem lo ratzitem l'kayeim mitzvotai", :gloss "and you did not wish to uphold My commandments"} {:he "על כן והריקותם אחריכם חרב", :translit "al ken v'harikotem achareichem charev", :gloss "therefore you emptied out after you sword"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והריקותי" "והריקותי לכם ברכה עד בלי די"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'והריקותי לכם ברכה עד בלי די' appears in Malachi 3:10 as a divine promise of overflowing blessing. The Ba'al HaTurim constructs a wordplay between that verse's והריקותי and the והריקותם of Leviticus 26:39, turning Israel's refusal to keep the commandments into the cause of the sword pursuing them.", :sources ["Malachi 3:10" "Leviticus 26:39"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The bent form of the letter zayin in 'ואתכם אזרה' signals a hidden link to the concept of seven (zayin = 7): seven nations, seven pillars of Torah, seven abominations.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["והריקותי" "והריקותי לכם ברכה עד בלי די"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "והריקותי", :refs ["Genesis 41:20" "Genesis 41:27" "Leviticus 26:33" "Malachi 3:10"], :n 4, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "והריקותי לכם ברכה עד בלי די", :refs ["Malachi 3:10"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:22.904116731Z", :model "glm-5.2"}